<title>LEBANON: Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 477.9 bln pounds.</title>
<headline>Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 477.9 bln pounds.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's weekly treasury bill issue of November 21 raised 477.9 billion Lebanese pounds, the finance ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The previous issue raised 375.9 billion pounds.</p>
<p>The new issue posted a nominal surplus of subscription against maturity of 254.6 billion pounds. It raised the following amounts (in billions of pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			  Yield		    Amount</p>
<p>    Three months	    14.43 (14.44)	   71.4  (55.8)</p>
<p>    Six months		16.67 (16.79)	   52.1  (63.3)</p>
<p>    12 months		 17.57 (17.64)	   84.2 (107.9)</p>
<p>    24 months		 21.26 (21.42)	  270.2 (148.9)</p>
<p>The Lebanese pound closed at 1,554.25 to the U.S. dollar on Monday from 1,555 a week earlier and 1,600 a year ago.</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602057 645456</p>
